// V2 of the registry API — the sole registry wire surface. Images are keyed by
// (workspace, extractor, tag); the v2 ContainerImage drops the legacy `name` field entirely in
// favour of extractor identity as the stable handle. The leaf types (FileExtractionInput,
// FileExtractionParameter, FileOutputFormat, TimestampMetadata, ContainerImageStatus, FileFilter,
// FileSuffix) live here now that the v1 surface has been deleted.
//
// V2 differs from the retired v1 surface in that:
//   - Images are keyed by (workspace, extractor, tag) instead of (workspace, name, tag).
//     Extractor identity replaces the user-supplied image name as the stable handle, so the
//     v2 ContainerImage type drops `name` entirely.
//   - The OCI repository path is {workspaceUuid}/{extractorUuid}:{tag}, replacing the legacy
//     {workspaceUuid}/{name}:{tag} layout.
//   - CreateImage requires extractor_rid, inputs, file_output_format so the registry has a
//     complete execution contract for the image, rather than relying on a separately persisted
//     record on the extractor that can drift from the image it points at.
//   - SearchFilter has no NameFilter (v2 images have no name to filter on); it exposes TagFilter,
//     StatusFilter, ExtractorFilter, and AndFilter.
//
// On the Java side, only CreateImage has its own service method (createImageV2): the OCI key,
// DB columns, and required metadata genuinely differ from the shared read path. GetImage /
// DeleteImage / SearchImages reuse the underlying RegistryService Java service methods, which
// now traffic in these v2 types directly.

